## Geometry and provenance distinctions

The three fig26a lattice nodes define its straight separator. Their collinearity determines its frame clips. Fig26b's two intercepts and independently supported positive-unit node define its separator and determine its frame clips. Fig27b's junction and two x-axis intersections determine the two complete diagonals and their four frame clips.

Fig27a's radius-2 circle, centered at its axis crossing, and vertical cutoffs one unit left/right determine chord-contact heights of plus/minus sqrt(3). These radicals, all computed clipping coordinates, and hatch-segment endpoints are analytic construction coordinates, not printed given values or visible answer labels.

Unlabeled source intersections use small ink anchors whose complete footprint is contained within existing heavy boundary/axis strokes. They do not introduce perceptible point dots or open/closed endpoint markers. This maps source relationships to the existing validator's point objects without claiming the source printed coordinate-pair labels. Additional frame-clip and guide-end construction points are explicitly `visible: false` and are not mapped as visible source objects.

Every mapped landmark, including the circle's four cardinal intersections and all four chord contacts, belongs to a mapped point-relationship assertion wholly inside its owning panel group. Each grid has its own `gridDimensions` group and exact assertion; 19 vertical positions / 13 horizontal positions delimit 18 / 12 cell intervals. Hidden construction points get separate assertion-only construction groups, not counterfeit printed-source claims.

## Deliberate modern regularization

- Arrange the two separate panels vertically rather than side by side. This changes layout only, not their individual coordinate frames.
- Use a 640 x 1024 canvas and `scroll` display with actual media width 640. One coordinate unit has the same horizontal/vertical scale. Minimum label size is 20 px at that width, exceeding the 16 px contract. Product integration and scroll reachability remain the parent's later checks.
- Move source panel captions outside the lattice and normalize them to `(a)` / `(b)`. Retain x/y axis names and certified scale labels. Do not transcribe the unreadable negative glyphs or add guessed labels in their place.
- Fig27b's clean upper `1` is explicitly a normalized scale label at the independently established one-unit junction, not a recovered literal source glyph.
- Use regular, moderately spaced deterministic hatching and leave small hatch-only clearances around numeric labels. The full instructional grid is retained. Hatch pitch and label clearances are modern additions, not exact source ink spacing.
- Preserve the mathematical boundaries as solid, with dashed horizontal guides only in fig26.
- Fig26b's positive guide has supported endpoints at the axis and the unit-height boundary node. The source's negative-level guide is only a supported short fragment; its clean one-unit horizontal extent left of the y axis is a deliberate guide regularization, not a certified source endpoint or additional inequality constraint.
- Do not show equations, inequalities, systems, ordered-pair annotations, radical values, radius annotations, or intersection names. No answer files are read.

## Stage and image budget

Use the existing validator and JSXGraph renderer without modifying either or hand-editing generated SVG/PNG. Preserve invocation receipts, input snapshots, outputs, and failures. At most one narrow content repair is authorized per figure; execution repairs do not erase attempts or image usage.

FIRST native source views remain 2, source reopens 0. New authorization is exactly one view of each final rendered PNG: 2 additional views, no reopens or other screenshots. Independent render review is still required after this author handoff. No `review@1` approval, promotion, modern-template edit, database, Git, environment setup, install, create, or attach operation is authorized.

## First-render layout repair

The first actual renderer call for each figure completed with exit 2 and a label-collision report, not an execution fault. Fig26b's origin `0` in the southeast position intersected the steep separator. Fig27b's upper `1` with an 18px west gap touched the padded diagonal footprint. Both reports independently measured 20px minimum text at width 640.

Each figure consumes its one authorized narrow content/layout repair: move fig26b's origin label to southwest, and increase fig27b's upper-label west gap to 26px. Update only the corresponding hatch-label clearances. Source hashes, all mathematical assertions, grid dimensions/phases, circle/chord geometry, separator locations, and untargeted objects are checked unchanged before writing. The original builder snapshot, original build record, first spec snapshots, failure reports, and unviewed first PNGs remain preserved. First PNGs were not opened; the two final-PNG view budget remains unused at the time of this repair.
